## Exit criteria

- [ ] Reproduce guidance audits each relevant join using the authors' actual
  keys on untouched inputs before normalization/cleaning, recording stage,
  keys, cardinality/duplication, match/unmatched diagnostics and denominators;
  preserve the original result and any separately labelled corrected run.
- [ ] Compare constructed variable definitions and sample rules in text,
  notes/appendices, and code; trace constructed missingness through operations
  and downstream samples. Unknown or conflicting evidence is recorded with
  source anchors as an anomaly, not an automatically established coding error.
- [ ] Evidence and unresolved audit coverage stay visible; author package
  files stay read-only. Findings/candidate corrections reuse existing signed
  probe and author-ruling rules rather than authorizing changed specifications.
- [ ] Person-written signatures, frozen comparison tolerance, existing
  selected-target/whole-paper/ACRe meanings, and report contracts stay unchanged.
  No new scientific run, score exception, default main-result rule, footnote
  scope ruling, or signing mode is introduced.

